  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 211 PM CDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nHigh pressure remains over the eastern half of the United States. \nWith the ridging not going anywhere any time soon, clear skies, very \nlight winds, and dry weather will continue across the state into the \nweekend. Overall, perfect weather for the latter half of harvest \nseason. The main focus of this forecast is the temperatures and lack \nof rain. \n\nTemperatures will continue to warm this week. Lows tonight will be \nin the mid 40s. Highs tomorrow into the weekend will range in the \nlow to upper 70s. Normals for this time of year is around 65-69 mid \nacross central and southeastern IL. Dry weather will last through \nthe extended period. \n\nLooks like a cold front will try to makes its way into IL around \nMonday, but with how dry the airmass is, it will have a hard fight \nto squeeze out any impacted rainfall as it passes. Chances for rain \nfor late weekend/early week is null.",
